    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **11 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on owners, formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nSince `GET /api/owners/{id}` (and the create response) serialize an `OwnerDto` produced by `OwnerMapper`, two coordinated changes were needed:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. The build's OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto` from this spec, so this gives the DTO its `displayName` getter/setter and includes the field in the JSON response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value via expression: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` (null-safe). This is applied wherever an owner is mapped to a DTO, including the `GET` that the acceptance test reads back.\n\nThe `Cp05Tests.coreComputesDisplayName` test passes (`$.displayName` == `\"<lastName>, John\"`), and all 11 tests across the suite remain green.",
